@Marafsol1 @ssssssssselim Mostly for US frontier models, not Chinese or non-frontier ones. Costs come down by 95% per year, so this is not an issue going forward. Plus most people now use other models (for example, I’m almost always on Opus 5.5, not Fable).

@YarnlerStiggums For most computer jobs the ability to understand and act across space and time is not relevant. For robots it is, and that's where world models come in. Fei Fei Li's company was just bought for something like $8B last week I believe, there is a reason for that.
